    "explanation": "Pinging the nearby gateway works and pinging the far server fails \u2014 that result splits the path in half and localizes the fault beyond the gateway, before any cable is touched. This is isolate-by-halves with a safe test, exactly the method the lesson teaches. Ping does not depend on DNS when an IP is used (A), nothing here indicates degradation rather than absence (C), and a single silent server has many causes of which conflict is only one (D).",
